// Pins that a distance must be greater than zero. A distance is a separation
// between the camera and what it looks at: zero puts the camera on that point
// and leaves no direction to look along, and a negative value puts it behind
// the point, which is not what the argument means.
//
// A negative value is the case pinned here rather than zero because it is the
// one that survives review unnoticed -- it looks like a deliberate number, and
// a sign error in an expression produces it silently. Zero is covered by the
// unit tests, which also cover -0.0.
@settings(experimentalFeatures = allow)

bad = view::oriented(view::Orientation::Front, distance = -50)
